<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">D. S. Senanayake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Don Stephen Senanayake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">D. S. Senanayake was a Sri Lankan politician who led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> to independence and served as its first prime minister from 1947 until his death in 1952. A founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-national-party">United National Party</a>, he promoted irrigation and peasant settlement in the dry zone. He died after a fall from his horse and was succeeded by his son Dudley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/d-s-senanayake.jpg" alt="D. S. Senanayake" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image is a work of an employee of the Government of Ceylon (Sri Lanka) / Scanned Edited &amp; Uploaded By MediaJet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_Photographic_Portrait_of_Don_Stephen_Senanayaka_(1884-1952).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
